# Cloudflare Pages SPA fallback.
#
# The app has no linking config, so every screen lives at `/` and this is not
# reached in normal use. It exists for the ways a browser arrives at a path
# anyway: a stray link, a refresh after a URL was typed, a crawler. Without it
# those get Cloudflare's 404 page, which looks like the deployment being
# broken rather than the URL being wrong.
#
# 200 rather than 301: the app should answer at whatever path was asked for,
# not send the browser somewhere else and lose the fragment. That matters —
# Supabase returns from an emailed link with `#access_token=…`, and a redirect
# is exactly how a fragment gets dropped.
/*    /index.html   200
